From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:36:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] hush: read: clear bb_got_signal before running the traps

With FEATURE_EDITING, record_pending_signo() sets bb_got_signal for
read_line_input() and the read builtin, but check_and_run_traps(),
which runs the traps, does not clear it; only the interactive line
input does. Once a non-interactive shell has run a trap, every poll of
shell_builtin_read() thus fails at once with EINTR, without a system
call, and builtin_read(), for which no trap is pending, retries forever:
read spins at full CPU, ie:

    trap 'echo USR1' USR1; kill -USR1 $$; read l < /proc/version

builtin_read() now clears bb_got_signal before it runs the traps of the
signals pending, a signal which comes later setting it again.

Upstream: not submitted
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
---
 shell/hush.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/shell/hush.c b/shell/hush.c
index dcc6b22..79f401d 100644
--- a/shell/hush.c
+++ b/shell/hush.c
@@ -11752,7 +11752,14 @@ static int FAST_FUNC builtin_read(char **argv)
 	r = shell_builtin_read(&params);
 
 	if ((uintptr_t)r == 1 && errno == EINTR) {
-		unsigned sig = check_and_run_traps();
+		unsigned sig;
+		/* The traps of the signals pending run here, and only line
+		 * input clears bb_got_signal: left set, it would make every
+		 * poll of shell_builtin_read() fail with EINTR. A signal
+		 * which comes after it is cleared sets it again.
+		 */
+		bb_got_signal = 0;
+		sig = check_and_run_traps();
 		if (sig != SIGINT)
 			goto again;
 	}
